quran[34]{c,v,t}:
  56,17,"Youths never altering in age will keep going around them,"
  56,18,"with goblets, pitchers and cups (full of pure wine) from flowing springs,"
  56,19,which will neither cause them headaches nor will they get intoxicated.
  56,20,"(They will be served) any fruit they choose,"
  56,21,and the meat of any bird they desire.
  56,22,"And (they will have) maidens with beautiful wide eyes,"
  56,23,"like pearls hidden in covers,"
  56,24,as a reward for what they used to do.
  56,25,"There, they will not hear any idle or sinful talk,"
  56,26,except the (virtuous) word: ‘Peace!’ ‘Peace!’
  56,27,"And the People of the Right Hand, how (blessed) are the People of the Right Hand!"
  56,28,"(They will be) among thornless lote trees,"
  56,29,"and banana trees clustered with fruits,"
  56,30,"and widely extended shades,"
  56,31,"and ever-flowing waters,"
  56,32,"and abundant fruits,"
  56,33,never out of season nor forbidden.
  56,34,And (they will be lodged) on raised floors (with noble spouses).
  56,35,"Indeed, We have created these (maidens) as a (unique) creation,"
  56,36,"and We made them virgins,"
  56,37,"loving, of matching age,"
  56,38,for the People of the Right Hand.
  56,39,"(There will be) a large group of them from the earlier generations,"
  56,40,and a large group from the later generations.
  56,41,"And the People of the Left Hand, how (miserable) are the People of the Left Hand!"
  56,42,"(They will be) in the hot, scorching wind and the boiling water (of Hell),"
  56,43,and the shadow of dense black smoke.
  56,44,(It is) neither cool nor refreshing.
  56,45,"Indeed, before that, they used to live in luxury,"
  56,46,and they would persist in great sin.
  56,47,"They used to say (mockingly): ‘When we are dead and become dust and bones, shall we be raised (alive again)?"
  56,48,And our forefathers of old (will also be given life)?’
  56,49,"Say: ‘Indeed, the former and later generations,"
  56,50,will (all) surely be gathered for the appointment of a known Day.
